e-football/story/_/id/50484151/darian-mensah-dices-ex-team-duke-miami-rebounds-first-loss","type":"HeadlineNews","byline":"Andrea Adelson","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"Wake Forest strengthens CFP case with 'statement' win at SMU","description":"No. 13 Wake Forest made a statement to the College Football Playoff selection committee with a 49-7 blowout of SMU on Saturday.","published":"2026-11-15T00:41:09.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/college-football/story/_/id/50483729/wake-forest-strengthens-cfp-case-statement-win-smu","type":"HeadlineNews","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"Vols lose top receiver Matthews to knee injury vs. Texas A&M","description":"Tennessee leading receiver Mike Matthews suffered a right knee injury in the second quarter of Saturday's game at Texas A&M.","published":"2026-11-14T23:16:10.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/college-football/story/_/id/50483677/vols-lose-top-receiver-matthews-knee-injury-vs-texas-am","type":"HeadlineNews","byline":"Mark Schlabach","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"Georgia commit, DL Marcellus Young Casario died after 'sudden medical emergency'","description":"Marcellus Young Casario, a Georgia football commit, died Friday after experiencing a \"sudden medical emergency,\" according to his high school.","published":"2026-11-14T20:36:58.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/college-football/story/_/id/50482223/georgia-football-commit-marcellus-young-casario-dies-suddenly","type":"HeadlineNews","byline":"Eli Lederman","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"Oklahoma AD rips Ole Miss, SEC; Rebels defend travel effort","description":"Oklahoma AD Roger Denny ripped the SEC and Ole Miss for the \"inexplicable\" decision to move its game to Sunday, while the Rebels defended their travel efforts.","published":"2026-11-14T23:54:22.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/college-football/story/_/id/50482206/oklahoma-ad-infuriated-sec-ole-miss-sunday-game","type":"HeadlineNews","byline":"Max Olson","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"Clemson QB Reynolds to have MRI on knee; backup Vizzina (ankle) also hurt","description":"Clemson quarterback Tait Reynolds is having an MRI on his injured knee, and backup Christopher Vizzina was sent to the hospital to evaluate his ankle.","published":"2026-11-14T23:52:45.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/college-football/story/_/id/50482105/clemson-qb-tait-reynolds-suffers-leg-injury-slide","type":"HeadlineNews","byline":"Andrea Adelson","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"Central Oklahoma AD trolls Ole Miss amid FAA crisis-forced kickoff change","description":"The Division II school offered Ole Miss fans attending its Oklahoma matchup free admission due to the kickoff date change.","published":"2026-11-14T22:28:10.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/college-football/story/_/id/50481529/central-oklahoma-troll-ole-miss-faa-decsion","type":"Story","byline":"Kalan Hooks","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"Ohio State WR Smith sets Big Ten record, states Heisman case","description":"Ohio State wide receiver Jeremiah Smith broke yet another record, eclipsing the Big Ten mark for career receiving yards while also making his Heisman Trophy case in Saturday's win over Northwestern.","published":"2026-11-14T23:15:02.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/college-football/story/_/id/50481134/ohio-state-jeremiah-smith-sets-big-ten-receiving-record","type":"HeadlineNews","byline":"Jake Trotter","source":"ESPN"}],"links":{"espn":"https://www.espn.com/college-football/player/_/id/4954453/cade-uluave","wikipedia":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cade_Uluave"},"wiki":{"rules":4,"title":"Cade Uluave","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cade_Uluave","description":"American football player (born 2005)","touched":"2026-11-14T07:35:54Z","intro":"Cade Uluave (born May 2, 2005) is an American college football linebacker for the BYU Cougars. He previously played for the California Golden Bears. He was named the Pac-12 Defensive Freshman of the Year in 2023.","sections":[{"key":"early","title":"Early life","text":"Uluave was born on May 2, 2005\n, and grew up in South Jordan, Utah."},{"key":"college","title":"College career","text":"CALIFORNIA\nUluave expected to see action on special teams as a true freshman at California in 2023, but after an injury to Jackson Sirmon he began to see extensive playing time on defense. He received Pac-12 Conference player of the week honors several times and finished the season with 13 games played, six as a starter. He was the leader in the conference among freshmen in tackles and tackles-for-loss (TFLs), totaling 66 tackles, 6.5 TFLs, 2.5 sacks, two interceptions, two forced fumbles and two fumble recoveries en route to being named the Pac-12 Defensive Freshman of the Year. He was selected third-team all-conference by Phil Steele and was named a freshman All-American.\nOn January 3, 2026, Uluave announced that he would enter the transfer portal.\n\nBYU\nOn January 13, 2026, Uluave announced that he would transfer to BYU."}]}}